    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters June 2nd with a focus on exploiting speed and platoon advantages. Our strongest play of the day is **Corbin Carroll** (77.40), who benefits from a favorable matchup against Lauer and a top-of-the-order slot that maximizes his stolen base potential. Close behind is **Jose Caballero** (70.71); while batting eighth carries a penalty, his dynamic platoon edge against the lefty Cantillo makes him a high-efficiency start in a category-scarcity league where his wheels are a primary target. **Tyler Soderstrom** (68.53) and **Gabriel Moreno** (64.94) also grade out as elite starts, taking advantage of favorable matchups against Lauer and Taillon respectively, solidifying our outfield and catching depth today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was leaving **Alex Freeland** (40.48) and **Cole Young** (40.40) on the bench. Both players hovered right at the edge of our marginal start threshold, but they ultimately failed to crack the lineup due to bottom-of-the-order defensive positioning and superior projected efficiency from the starters currently ahead of them. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the status of **Mickey Moniak**, who remains on the IL, and **Josh Naylor**, who is currently out of the lineup. We are wary of **Dalton Rushing** (44.91) and **Travis Bazzana** (44.58) as they face tougher-than-average arms in Soroka and Schlittler, respectively; their starts are prioritized more for volume than elite efficiency, so we will be watching their early at-bats closely to ensure our daily game caps aren't being wasted on stagnating production.",
